IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aca-dates`

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic) -- the amounts: the figures printed in the Act, and the figures as varied under
-- Division 2D of Part IV for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027.
--
-- THE ACT'S FIGURES. Division 2D varies the listed amounts "in respect of the financial year beginning on 1 July 2014 and
-- each subsequent financial year" (ss 100B, 100C), starting from the amount printed in column 2 of the Table. So the
-- figures the Act prints are read as those in force immediately before 1 July 2014 (NOTES.md fork F3). Amounts no longer
-- in the Table to s 100C (the s 98C(2)(b)-(d), (3)(b), (c) and (4) figures: their items are shown "* * * * *") are not
-- varied, and are used as printed.
--
-- THE VARIED FIGURES. Not in the Act. They are taken from the Accident Compensation Act 1985 notice in Victoria Government
-- Gazette No. S 363 of 30 June 2026, deposited at
-- subjects/au/vic/workers-compensation-annual-indexation-notice/registers/source-bundle/GG2026S363.txt (text lines 9-336),
-- the instrument that sets the numbers this Act uses. The stable l4 cannot IMPORT across subject folders, so the figures
-- are copied here with their line, never recomputed. Each pair is "Rate before 1 July 2026" then "Rate from 1 July 2026".
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from plain-text conversions by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Act (Version No.
-- 237) and of the Gazette's PDF. (c) State of Victoria. Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
-- (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Amounts`

§§ `The weekly payment ceilings -- ss 93A, 93B, 93C, 93CD(5), with s 100B items 1-12, 15, 16`

-- The three kinds of claim the weekly payment sections distinguish (s 93A(1)-(3), s 93B(1)-(3), s 93C(2), s 93CD(5)).
DECLARE `Weekly payments claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant`
    `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010`
    `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010`

-- The Act prints $1210 (pre-12 November 1997 claimants) and $1510 (claims from 12 November 1997 to before 5 April 2010);
-- claims from 5 April 2010 are capped at "twice the State average weekly earnings" (a term of the 2013 Act, s 5(2)(a)).
-- Gazette lines 172-190 (and the same figures at 191-254): "$1,700 $1,740" (before 12 November 1997); "$2,150 $2,200" (on
-- or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010); "$2,930 $3,000" (on or after 5 April 2010).
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim`, `the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly payment ceiling for` `the claim` `in the week of` `the week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` THEN `on` `the week` `the amount printed` 1700 `or` 1740
    WHEN `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` THEN `on` `the week` `the amount printed` 2150 `or` 2200
    WHEN `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` THEN `on` `the week` `the amount printed` 2930 `or` 3000

-- s 93CA(1)(c), s 93CD(4)(a), s 93CDA(1)(d): "$177 per week" (s 100B items 13, 14, 17). Gazette lines 222-226, 254:
-- "$251 $257".
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 93CD(4)(a) minimum weekly earnings on` `the day` MEANS `on` `the day` `the amount printed` 251 `or` 257

§§ `Damages -- s 134AB(22) and s 135A(7), with s 100B items 19, 20 and s 100C items 45-50`

-- Gazette lines 304-316.
--   134AB(22)(a)(i) Threshold $77,490 $79,890     134AB(22)(a)(ii) Maximum $1,744,530 $1,798,500
--   134AB(22)(b)(i) Threshold $74,820 $77,130     134AB(22)(b)(ii) Maximum $759,510 $783,000
--   135A(7)(a)(i)   Threshold $85,350 $87,360     135A(7)(a)(ii)   Maximum $1,921,400 $1,966,550
--   135A(7)(b)(i)   Threshold $69,300 $71,440     135A(7)(b)(ii)   Maximum $703,460 $725,220
-- The Act prints, before variation: s 134AB(22) $56 650, $1 275 570, $54 730, $555 350; s 135A(7) $59 670, $1 343 540,
-- $50 680, $514 360.
DECLARE `Damages section` IS ONE OF
    `section 134AB`
    `section 135A`

DECLARE `Head of damages` IS ONE OF
    `pecuniary loss damages`
    `pain and suffering damages`

DECLARE `Damages limits` HAS
    `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the section` IS A `Damages section`, `the head` IS A `Head of damages`, `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Damages limits`
`the damages limits under` `the section` `for` `the head` `on` `the day of the award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amounts year of` `the day of the award`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: no deposited notice for that year)
    WHEN JUST `the year` THEN
        CONSIDER `the section`
        WHEN `section 134AB` THEN
            CONSIDER `the head`
            WHEN `pecuniary loss damages` THEN JUST (`Damages limits` WITH
                `the threshold` IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 77490 `or` 79890
                `the maximum`   IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 1744530 `or` 1798500)
            WHEN `pain and suffering damages` THEN JUST (`Damages limits` WITH
                `the threshold` IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 74820 `or` 77130
                `the maximum`   IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 759510 `or` 783000)
        WHEN `section 135A` THEN
            CONSIDER `the head`
            WHEN `pecuniary loss damages` THEN JUST (`Damages limits` WITH
                `the threshold` IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 85350 `or` 87360
                `the maximum`   IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 1921400 `or` 1966550)
            WHEN `pain and suffering damages` THEN JUST (`Damages limits` WITH
                `the threshold` IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 69300 `or` 71440
                `the maximum`   IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 703460 `or` 725220)

§§ `Non-economic loss -- s 98C, with s 100C items 23-25, 28-30`

-- As printed in s 98C (not varied: their Table items are gone).
--   (2)(b)(i)  "$11 670 + [(D - 10) $9940]"            (2)(c)(i), (3)(b) "$18 810 + [(D - 10) $2830]"
--   (2)(d), (3)(c) "$75 260 + [(D - 30) $4700]"        (4) "$67 660"
`s 98C(2)(b) base` MEANS 11670
`s 98C(2)(b) per point` MEANS 9940
`s 98C(2)(c) base` MEANS 18810
`s 98C(2)(c) per point` MEANS 2830
`s 98C(2)(d) base` MEANS 75260
`s 98C(2)(d) per point` MEANS 4700
`s 98C(4) amount for loss of a foetus` MEANS 67660

-- s 98C(2)(e)(i), (3)(d)(i) "$262 070 + [(D - 70) $29 330]", (2)(e)(ii), (f), (3)(d)(ii), (e) "$555 350": varied (s 100C
-- items 23-25, 28-30). The relevant date for a rating over 70% is "the date on which the calculation is made" (s 98C(1A)).
-- Gazette lines 270-283: "98C(2)(e)(i) Where the worker's impairment benefit rating is more than 70% and not more than 80%
-- $358,420 $369,510 / $40,120 $41,360"; "98C(2)(e)(ii) Maximum amount ... $759,510 $783,000"; "98C(2)(f) ... more than 80%
-- $759,510 $783,000"; the same for 98C(3)(d), (e).
DECLARE `Upper band figures` HAS
    `the base over 70`      IS A NUMBER
    `the amount per point`  IS A NUMBER
    `the upper maximum`     IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Upper band figures`
`the s 98C upper band figures on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amounts year of` `the day of the calculation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: no deposited notice for that year)
    WHEN JUST `the year` THEN JUST (`Upper band figures` WITH
        `the base over 70`     IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 358420 `or` 369510
        `the amount per point` IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 40120 `or` 41360
        `the upper maximum`    IS `in` `the year` `the amount printed` 759510 `or` 783000)

-- s 98C(11): "a worker is not entitled to an amount of compensation for non-economic loss under this section or section
-- 98E or both that exceeds the maximum amount payable under this section as in force at the date of the relevant injury."
-- The maximum the Act prints, $555 350, is read as the maximum in force from 1 July 2013 to 30 June 2014 (fork F3). For an
-- injury before 1 July 2013 the maximum then in force is not in the deposit: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 98C(11) maximum for an injury on` `the day of the injury` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `falls from` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2013) `to` (`the calendar date` 30 6 2014)
    THEN JUST 555350
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the maximum in force at that date is in an earlier version)
